course: dictionary
lesson: 325
title: Angrily and how we say things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Angrily tells you the way someone does something. It comes from angry, and it describes an action: «shouted angrily» tells you the shouting was done in an angry way.
explain: The word helps you read a character's feelings. «slammed the door angrily» shows the person feels cross or mad, and the slammed door shows how strong that feeling is.
explain: Feeling angry is fine, but acting angrily can hurt people. Try to breathe, count to ten, and then talk calmly. «Nicknames usually fade faster if you don't react angrily.»
fact: Angrily means in an angry way, showing that you feel cross or mad.
fact: Angrily is an adverb: it tells us how something is done, as in «shouted angrily».
fact: «They argued about it at dinner, not angrily, just properly.» Here not angrily means calmly, without being cross.
fact: «"durnyk" means "silly, dummy"; among friends it is said laughing, but said angrily it hurts.»
fact: Feeling angry is allowed, but acting angrily is a choice you can avoid.
exercise: «She slammed the door angrily.» What does angrily tell us? | In a happy, laughing way | Very quietly and slowly | Before she went to bed | *In an angry way, showing she felt cross
exercise: «They argued about it at dinner, not angrily, just properly.» What does not angrily mean here? | *Calmly, without being cross | Furiously and loudly | Sadly, with tears in their eyes
exercise: Which word tells you how someone shouts when they feel cross? | Happily | Quietly | *Angrily | Sleepily
test: «"durnyk" said laughing between friends is a joke, but said angrily it hurts.» What makes the word hurt? | Said in a sing-song voice | Said quietly after school | Written on a piece of paper | *Said in an angry way
test: When you feel angry, what is the best thing to do? | *Breathe, count to ten, then talk calmly | Slam the door angrily | Shout as loud as you can
exam: «Nicknames from an embarrassing moment usually fade within weeks, and faster if you don't react angrily.» Why do nicknames fade faster? | They are never used at school | Because the teacher bans them | *Because you don't react angrily | Because they are written down
